{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-integral-dim-up}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-dimension-going-up}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-integral-going-up}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0cfef3fdaffad7b63a3c1663499a89d928aba23b343cb4b42a9ce4d330c9149", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ee96f3bb10690c99bb827f8e0bd468dd5cc9a0361c53b71185b2557ccf3d6344", "source_text": "Since the dimension of <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> is the supremum of the dimensions\nof the members of an affine open covering, we may assume <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004>\nare affine. The inequality follows from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe equality then follows from\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ad33a0a335b29be335876337320b19c034285d7d3a684f5fdef663684b51a33d", "unit_id": "tag:0ECG:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-quasi-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cda481fcaaa8ddbb1f993903b50c342d73b16303e00e55eed5a0cc2f8b5f683d", "source_text": "A finite morphism is quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f77d07df0922b280c9b493d7b66215bba15d97381675b4c527b0087f9f452a52", "unit_id": "tag:02NU:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-quasi-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-locally-quasi-compact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-integral-fibres}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:279e585fea053173bfe0218b5bc151d1ff2f15575fb07fc54587b196b74cb323", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6875816ad325fb61f52b61198d2c769cb5c599a22d1d853bc9254b53db52b3e9", "source_text": "This is implied by Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand Lemma <REF_0002>.\nAlternatively, all points in fibres are closed points by\nLemma <REF_0003> (and the fact that a finite\nmorphism is integral) and use\nLemma <REF_0004> (3) to\nsee that <MATH_0001> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0002> for all <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:753e14841fff0e473e38d2235e9531f2d748b851f0adfff525880d0b7b893b2e", "unit_id": "tag:02NU:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:91f7f690005974538f9413d26e06567c7aaac53ad99387d497b14ae3e3c887e8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d794f3ee149616c40c0bcf3f2baa4dc5d880bd007f7235c5912c087d489e3706", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is finite, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is affine and proper.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1d75b9102e4054fb53184a57e2f490aa2389448422228a7718c76d55ce3e548", "unit_id": "tag:01WN:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-integral-universally-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-integral}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:721c6eb3f7d6a283b373e52e406d4bc1c2bc49884758c31dd9d24a2c0b3a8773", "source_text": "This follows formally from\nLemma <REF_0001>,\nthe fact that a finite morphism is integral and separated,\nthe fact that a proper morphism is the same thing as\na finite type, separated, universally closed morphism,\nand the fact that an integral morphism of finite type is\nfinite (Lemma <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e7fb701ef07fd3bbef6ad72719d28461776fe025209896d2de21f3b9c3dbb168", "unit_id": "tag:01WN:proof"}
